    "created_at": "2024-06-10T16:05:36Z",
    "updated_at": "2024-06-10T16:05:36Z",
    "body": "> I think one change I'd like to see is that we drop \"cross-origin\" from the internal naming scheme now that we make it apply to same-origin scenarios\r\n\r\nWould it make sense to spin off this editorial only change to a separate PR? (happy to work on it, just wondering RE editorial vs. functional split)\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n> * obtain a cross-origin opener policy\r\n\r\nOops, added!\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n> * check if COOP values require a browsing context group switch\r\n\r\nI *think* this is covered by the change to [matching COOP](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/browsers.html#matching-coop), but I could be I'm missing something..",
