    "created_at": "2024-08-07T11:27:18Z",
    "updated_at": "2024-08-07T11:27:18Z",
    "body": "> @arturjanc - should I understand from your [comment](https://gist.github.com/yoavweiss/c7b61e97e6f8d207be619f87ab96ead5?permalink_comment_id=5092478#gistcomment-5092478) that you'd like to see something more explicit here?\r\n\r\nYes, I think it could be helpful to at least add a note somewhere saying that browser should aim to put documents with this COOP value in a separate renderer process (or something along these lines) -- otherwise, same-origin documents would still be able to read arbitrary from memory even if they can't directly access it using web-level APIs.",
